                <pb facs="0253" n="204" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76v20/pg204"/>

                <head>100. Memorandum From the President’s Assistant for National Security Affairs
                    (Kissinger) to President Nixon </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1970-12-01">December 1, 1970</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <note rend="inline" type="source">[Source: National Archives, Nixon Presidential
                    Materials, NSC Files, Box 29, President’s Daily Briefs. Top Secret; Sensitive;
                    Codeword. Excerpt—1 page of source text not declassified. A notation in
                    President Nixon’s handwriting in the margin of this memorandum reads: “K—a
                    disturbing report—Perhaps we need a stronger Ambassador.”]</note>
            </div>
        </body>
